<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Worship in the heart (Source/ColonyCouncil/Gods/Worship/; docs/design/gods.md, "Worship": the heart). Kept small, as the
    balance targets ask: a prayer said and an offering carried give no mood but something else (RewardInstead: hope, a
    little awe, a felt good moment); the god's dream gives awe; only an answer or a prayer that came good, and a kept vow,
    are good moods, and they are rare (WorshipMath.AnswerChance, a few vows a colony-year). The setbacks are an unanswered
    prayer that became a crisis of faith (about a third of the unanswered), a broken vow, and a scoffer's mockery; the
    couples' bickering over whose god sent the rain is an opinion, not a mood. Modelled in Tools/Balance (Rates.Worship).
  -->

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Prayed</defName>
    <durationDays>0.5</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>said a prayer</label>
        <description>I said what I needed to say to my god. Whether anyone heard it or not, I feel steadier for having said it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><feelings><li>Hope</li></feelings><felt>2</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Offered</defName>
    <durationDays>0.5</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>left an offering</label>
        <description>I carried the gift out and set it down where the god would find it. It's a small thing, and it felt right.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><feelings><li>Contentment</li></feelings><felt>1</felt></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Answered</defName>
    <durationDays>3</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>my prayer was answered</label>
        <description>I asked, and it came. Say what you like about chance. I know who I thank.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Unanswered</defName>
    <durationDays>4</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>a crisis of faith</label>
        <description>I prayed and prayed, and nothing. Either nobody is listening, or my god turned away from me. I don't know which is worse.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_VowKept</defName>
    <durationDays>3</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>kept my vow</label>
        <description>I swore it, and I did it, every day of it. My god saw, and so did everyone else.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_MemoryBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_VowBroken</defName>
    <durationDays>5</durationDays>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>broke my vow</label>
        <description>I swore it before my god and I broke it. I can't look at the shrine.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Mocked</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>1.5</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>mocked my faith</label>
        <description>I saw what my god did with my own eyes, and they laughed at me for it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-2</baseMoodEffect>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-8</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Worship_Bickered</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>argued over whose god sent the rain</label>
        <description>It was my god, plainly. We'll be arguing about this at supper for a week.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-3</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef ParentName="Council_DreamBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Dream_God</defName>
    <durationDays>0.8</durationDays>
    <stages><li><label>dreamt of my god</label><description>It wasn't like other dreams. I woke knowing who had spoken, and what was said.</description><baseMoodEffect>0</baseMoodEffect></li></stages>
    <modExtensions><li Class="ColonyCouncil.RewardInstead"><feelings><li>Awe</li></feelings><felt>2</felt><inspiration>0.03</inspiration></li></modExtensions>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!-- What helps (the Mood tab and the council's Moods page). -->

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_Worship_Unanswered</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Rimfolk_Worship_Unanswered</li></thoughts>
    <fix>It passes with time. A priest's word, a prayer that comes good, or a festival kept for their god all steady them; two crises in a month and they may turn to another god.</fix>
    <act>Passes with time</act>
    <actionable>false</actionable>
    <article>Council_Alm_C_Worship</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_Worship_VowBroken</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Rimfolk_Worship_VowBroken</li></thoughts>
    <fix>It passes with time. For a vow of no meat, keep vegetarian meals in the stores while it lasts, and let them keep to them in their food policy.</fix>
    <act>Passes with time</act>
    <actionable>false</actionable>
    <article>Council_Alm_C_Worship</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

  <ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Mood_Worship_Mocked</defName>
    <thoughts><li>Rimfolk_Worship_Mocked</li></thoughts>
    <fix>It passes in a day or two. Scoffers mock what the believers saw; keeping the two apart at the god's place, or a word between them, keeps it from festering.</fix>
    <act>Passes with time</act>
    <actionable>false</actionable>
    <article>Council_Alm_C_Worship</article>
  </ColonyCouncil.MoodHintDef>

</Defs>
